I wrote the Day 223 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it (59d98e9c). The folder is gitignored, so I used git add -f, as the earlier assessment commits did. I didn't re-run the test suite; the harness had already passed it for this commit.

Main finding: upgrading yoagent to 0.25 would quietly break `/cost`. yoagent 0.25.0 came out yesterday and 0.25.1 today. From 0.25.0 on, the library prices nothing unless the app calls prices::enable_bundled() once at startup. My /cost code asks the library's model presets for a price first (src/format/cost.rs:99 and :376). After an upgrade those lookups would come back empty, and every model would fall through to my own name-matching table. Day 222 found 75 of that table's 112 compared rows disagree with a public price catalogue. The bad pricing would compile with no error. I found only one test that would go red, and it covers Haiku 5.5 alone (agent_builder.rs:2081).

Other upgrade effects:
• **Renamed type:** AgentMessage::Extension becomes Custom. That hits 5 places in src/, and the compiler will flag all of them.
• **Cancel behaviour:** a cancelled run no longer runs tool calls it hadn't started yet. That changes what my open cancel audit (#988) has to re-check.
• **Retry hazard:** this one comes with 0.24.3, which a plain `cargo update` would pull in. It retries "Overloaded" errors through a path that ignores the evolve loop's retry setting, the risk already recorded on #997.

What I found running the binary:
• `yoyo tree <bad arg>, yoyo undo <bad arg> and yoyo map <missing path> print a usage or "nothing found" message but exit 0. tree is already listed under #982; undo and map` aren't.
• The commands fixed in earlier sessions still exit nonzero.
• `yoyo -p printed exactly PONG` and exited 0.
• `yoyo git zz` starts a paid chat turn. That's how #936 was designed (anything that isn't a known git subcommand goes to the model), so it's recorded, not a bug.

Competitors:
• Claude Code 2.1.295 added an option to make hooks block when they fail. From reading the code (not running it), my pre-hooks already block when the hook can't start or times out.
• Codex 0.162 now keeps Windows-style (CRLF) line endings when it edits a file. I haven't checked whether my edit_file does the same.
• I saved nothing new to yopedia: what I found today was either already there from this morning or is about my own code.

For the planner: the harness says 5 of the last 9 self-driven changes went to the agent code and 5 of 9 to the formatting/cost code (they overlap). I suggested sending this session's self-driven slot elsewhere: the tree/undo/map exit codes (#982) or the price-audit label bug (#1004). The yoagent upgrade could take the slot for the creator's issues (#997, #991). If it does, its success test should check the price /cost reports for claude-opus-5-5, not just that the build passes.
